  "text": "Recipe: Jowar Muttige\nCreator: Prathima Kharvi\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: jowar flour, sorghum flour, crushed garlic, dhaniya (coriander leaves), jeera powder, cumin powder, paprika, chili powder\nCooking methods: cook, no-cook\nInstructions: JOWAR ROTI: Prepare jowar roti (circular flatbread) with jowar flour (sorghum flour).\nSPICE MIX: Combine crushed garlic (small piece), dhaniya (coriander leaves), jeera powder (cumin powder), paprika or chili powder.\nJOWAR MUTTIGE: Combine the Spice Mix with hot Jowar Roti. Pound it again & shape into a ball.\nNotes: Jowar roti should be hot from tawa. Otherwise those balls will turn dry and won't be so tasty. A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (jowar flour | sorghum flour), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
